{
  "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
  "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stewart",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0000-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 202(h) of the Telecommunications Act of 1996 reflects Congress's conclusion that in light of intervening competitive developments, broadcast cross-ownership restrictions adopted in an earlier era may no longer be warranted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the FCC has devised other programs, like the incubator program and the eligibility -- eligible entity definition, that are intended to give certain regulatory advantages to small entities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Mr. Stewart, can I just interrupt and ask another question before my time elapses? Do you see a difference between a stated goal of enhancing minority and female ownership and not harming minority and female ownership, and if so, which is the FCC's?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The FCC concluded that because a variety of alternative media voices are now available to consumers, the viewpoint diversity concerns that originally prompted the cross-ownership rules were far less acute today."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yet, the Third Circuit vacated the order because the Commission failed to adequately consider minority and female ownership."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Do you agree that\nif the term is \"public interest\" in isolation,\nthat an agency has discretion to interpret that\nto encompass effects on women and minority\nownership?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: So, Ms. Walker,\ngiven that Congress wanted this statute to be a\nvehicle for deregulation, not more regulation,\nis it your position that the word \"modify\" in\n202(h), when it requires the Commission to\nmodify or repeal as part of its quadrennial\nreview, that a modification can never be an\nadditional regulatory requirement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Thank you, Mr. Chief\nJustice.\nCounsel, I'm just a bit confused.\nPetitioners indicate that in the past, these\nstructural ownership rules simply did not\ninclude minority and female ownership\nconsiderations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Ms. Deutsch, you began\nyour argument today by saying that the\ngovernment agrees with you that minority and\nfemale ownership should be taken into account in\ndecision-making like this. But as I understand\nwhat the government has done this morning is to\nsay that we -- that they don't agree with you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: So, Ms. Deutsch, suppose that that's right, and the --the Commission has historically considered this as -- as one factor in its broader public interest analysis, but, here, the Commission says something along the lines of: Look, there's actually not a lot of data about how this rule will affect minority and female ownership. To the extent that we have data, we think it's -- it -- it shows that it won't have an impact, and -- and so we're going to go with this new rule. Why -- why isn't that enough?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Deutsch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DEUTSCH: Because it would be an important break with past commitments, not only the repeated promise to -- to collect data and analyze this problem, which, as I said, goes back to the 1995 TV rule, but --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Deutsch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DEUTSCH: The Commission has its own data already that it collects in the Form 323, for instance. So, no, I'm not saying that, but I think what was wrong with your first formulation or how it might have been, you know, more passable was if the Commission had said: We can't figure it out. It's too uncertain. Put to one side our promises about figuring it out better. But we're willing to move forward no matter the harm to this goal, even though we still think this goal is important, but we --we just -- you know, we're throwing up our hands."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Let me ask you a -- a question about the retention of jurisdiction here. I understand that courts obviously have the practice of sometimes deferring to -- to another court and -- and -- and consolidating matters voluntarily, but what authority is there for the Third Circuit to have retained jurisdiction over not one rule-making but now three over the course of 15 years? That does seem a little unusual in its duration and in the number of rule-makings involved. I think Judge Williams called it contrary to the goals of Congress."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Deutsch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DEUTSCH: Well, Justice Gorsuch, our -- our view is that it's a proper exercise of that court's jurisdiction, and the government never challenged it below. It -- it happens sometimes, although not frequently, for -- for similar cases that have long and complicated histories and also a history of agency delay."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Deutsch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DEUTSCH: Well, certainly, the Free Press study which is cited in our brief and cited by the government in its analysis. And I would also point you to one of the early reviews where the Commission itself represent -- recognized the drop in minority and female ownership after the consolidation in the late '90s, and that's cited in our brief at 10 at 15 FCCR at 11084."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Deutsch",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "16b7409ca828bb551bb32c7ee4edc5382faa9059fb9c65ea0fa483295f75ce69",
      "evidence_id": "ev-16b7409ca828-0003-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. DEUTSCH: I -- I don't think it went so far as that, but it was an inference that could be drawn from that analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2020-19-1231",
